  "body": "The current failure message is a very non-obvious complaint that '@&#8203;' isn't a valid user identifer. This fails because of the implementation quirk in Python that any string is iterable as a list of one-character substrings.\n\nIdeally, a invite \"list\" of a single string should instead return an error message to the effect that it was expecting a list, got a string. That would immediately alert the unwary client developer to this fact.\n\n(Imported from https://matrix.org/jira/browse/SYN-331)\n\n(Reported by @leonerd)",
